<a name="1"></a><strong>What is Pay Per Click Payment Rotation?</strong><br>
Ad Payment Rotation is how we decide the order and amount of times your campaign is seen by our site visitors. The more you pay for each click the more your banner will be run within the rotation. For example, if you bid $0.75 per click and another person bids $0.25 per click, your banner will be seen 3 times more often by the site visitors than the person bidding $0.25. But no matter how many times your banner is seen, you still only have to pay for traffic sent directly to your site.
<br><br>
<a name="2"></a><strong>What Does Pay Per Click Mean?</strong><br>
Pay Per Click means you only have to pay for advertising if a visitor clicks on a banner at our sites to get to yours. So if your campaign is seen by 10 people before it gets clicked on or 3,000 before it gets clicked on, you still only pay what you bid on for that single click.
<br><br>
<a name="3"></a><strong>What are Campaigns?</strong><br>
A campaign is a series of banners targeting a group of websites. So if you have $500.00 to spend and want to have 3 different banners target both Brainburst.com and PlayorDraw.com at $0.35 per click we would set up 1 Campaign to rotate your 3 banners evenly across those sites for you. After your banner is clicked on 1,429 ($500.00 / .35) your campaign would expire and move out of the rotation.
<br><br>
<a name="4"></a><strong>Which Sites Can I Target with my Campaigns?</strong><br>
This system currently allows you to target as many of the following Trading Card Game Sites as you want for each campaign you run:
<br>
<ul>
<li><a href="http://www.brainburst.com/" target=_new>Brainburst.com</a></li>
<li><a href="http://www.duelyugioh.com/" target=_new>Duelyugioh.com</a></li>
<li><a href="http://www.playordraw.com/" target=_new>Playordraw.com</a></li>
<li><a href="http://www.pokeschool.com/" target=_new>Pokeschool.com</a></li>
<li><a href="http://www.vsuniverse.com/" target=_new>Vsuniverse.com</a></li>
<li><a href="http://www.tcgplayer.com/" target=_new>Tcgplayer.com</a></li>
</ul>
So if you want to target VSUniverse.com and PlayorDraw.com with your campaign, you can. Or, if you would like to target just DuelYuGiOh.com that is also no problem.
<br><br>
<a name="5"></a><strong>Can I Have Multiple Banners for a Single Campaign?</strong><br>
You are able to use as many banners as you want for each campaign. So if you want to use 3 different banners for your campaign targeting Brainburst.com and VSUniverse.com, you can. Once a campaign has begun however, you will not be able to adjust the banners.
<br><br>
<a name="6"></a><strong>Can I have More than 1 Campaign?</strong><br>
Yes. It is possible to have one campaign targeting just Brainburst.com, another targeting VSUniverse.com and a third targeting both DuelYuGiOh.com and Pokeschool.com. <br><br>
<a name="7"></a><strong>What Are the Banner Specifications?</strong><br>
We are currently allowing only Super Banners for this system. These particular banners are located at the top of each site and are 728x90 in size. If we have demand for Skyscrapers (120x600) then we will allow those to have campaigns targeted at thema s well.
<br><br>
<a name="8"></a><strong>Can I View Statistics?</strong><br>
Yes. All statistics are in real time and allow you to view how well each banner and campaign is doing. You will be provided with a login and password that allows you to view stats on all of your campaigns and the banners within those campaigns. You can even have statistics automatically emailed to you each night or week.
<br><br>
<a name="9"></a><strong>Can I Adjust My Campaign Once it has Started?</strong><br>
No. This is a new system and does not allow for the modification of campaigns once they begin. Once an agreement is made on a campaign it is run <u>as is</u> until it expires. In the future we may allow banners to be changed out or bid amounts lowered or raised. Our advice is to start off with a small total amount for your first campaign if you are not familiar to this type of system. This will allow you to see how quickly or slowly you are receiving visitors and to adjust the amount you spend per click for future campaigns. Please remember, that you only pay for visitors to your site. So if you believe you put too low a bid in per click for your first campaign you can always choose a larger per click amount for future campaigns.
<br><br>
